    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-16T21:17:48+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-16T21:17:48+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-16T11:47:48Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-16T11:47:48Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system southeast of the state slowly drifts further to the southeast over Tasmania today and is forecast to be located in the Tasman Sea on Monday, while extending a ridge over much of South Australia through to Tuesday. A trough of low pressure over Queensland pushes into the far northeast of SA until Monday, as another trough moves into far southwestern parts later on Tuesday and moves southeast across the state into Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW011" description="Eastern Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-16T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-16T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning northeasterly during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:30am to 2:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 4 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm near the coast in the afternoon. Winds northerly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending westerly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 18 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm near the coast in the morning. The chance of morning fog. Light winds becoming south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the day then becoming light during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching around 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
